From: Your Name <godkiller_nt@hammermaps.de>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 09:36:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix ScoreCover scoring an unknown enemy, found via activity
 log analysis

Analyzed the ai_hybrid_log.jsonl activity log from a c2a5f playtest
(16,301 entries, 41 grunts, ~230s): confirmed the Phase C squad-shared
confidence floor fires correctly (379 entries at confidence ~0.70
while not directly visible) and ATTACK never fires without visibility
(0 violations across the whole log) - but 9,395 of 10,227 COVER log
entries turned out to be a false-positive baseline with confidence
exactly 0, before any enemy was ever encountered.

Root cause: ScoreCover() lacked the `!memory.enemyKnown -> 0` guard
ScoreSearch() already had, so a cautious-leaning default AIProfile
(caution*30 - aggression*15 > 0) always scored COVER above zero even
with no enemy known. Harmless in-game (ResolveHybridSchedule()'s
m_hEnemy == NULL check already blocked a real schedule from ever
resulting), but a genuine utility-AI modeling gap and misleading in
the debug/activity log. Fixed with the same guard, updated tests.

Also deleted a 204MB stray ai_hybrid_log.jsonl that had accumulated
at the Half-Life root before spserver.cfg fixed the log path.

Verified: all core tests pass, client.so/vgui.so byte-identical to
the pre-Phase-A baseline (only hl.so differs). Phase C's manual
playtest (this log analysis) is now confirmed and closed out in
docs/designs/hybrid-ai-core-phase-c.md.

